WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:23.050
In this review, I’m not gonna tell you that
the iPhone 11 Pro is the best iPhone ever

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.050
made.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:25.050
It obviously is.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.540
I’m also not gonna reverbatate all of the
specs, like you’ve heard a thousand times

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.540
already.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:34.660
What I’m gonna talk about are the things
that actually matter, to both a tech enthusiast

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.980
and an average consumer, like my wife.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.120
Both of us have been using the iPhone 11 Pro
for a few days now, so I’ve collected my

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.710
own thoughts and I also interviewed my wife
to see what differences she noticed and what

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:48.040
she liked about the iPhone 11 Pro.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.100
But before I get into that, let’s talk about
what happened at Apple’s event.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.019
There’s no doubt that a lot of people were
a bit disappointed.

00:00:55.019 --> 00:00:58.940
A lot of people argued that Apple shouldn’t
have used the name “Pro”, since it’s

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:05.979
missing a few Pro features like 120hz refresh
rate, a USB-C port and reverse wireless charging,

00:01:05.979 --> 00:01:09.350
but after people started to get the 11 Pro
in their hands..

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.480
The disappointment started to fade away.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:16.110
So the question is, does it matter that the
new iPhone is missing a few Pro features that

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.660
Apple fans were anticipating?

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.710
For most people, not really.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:25.430
What it does pack is a few important features
and changes that make it a seriously good

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:29.050
package overall in terms of being a premium
smartphone.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:32.840
It now packs all 3 camera lenses that you’d
hope to see in a smartphone.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:38.530
It now packs night mode, which as you’ll
see later, works incredibly well.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.930
It packs the best processor in any smartphone.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:43.210
It has top-of-the-line battery life.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:47.120
A high-quality display that’s even brighter
this year.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.580
Incredibly balanced speakers.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:51.360
It finally comes with a fast charger in the
box.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.460
It packs top-of-the-line security.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.910
And it features a truly unique design that
you’ll never confuse for anything else.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:02.950
It seems as though for the first time in a
long time, the iPhone 11 Pro gives you a complete

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:14.950
package of features, and that’s what truly
matters.

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:19.580
When it comes to upgrading your iPhone, I
thought of a formula for iPhone upgradability

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.400
that is more realistic for regular consumers.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.730
And offering a full package of features that
work very well together is the first piece

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:27.730
of the puzzle.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:31.090
Second, the iPhone has to look and feel different.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:35.740
Not that many people upgraded from the iPhone
X to the XS, and that’s because it looked

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:38.019
basically identical to the X.

00:02:38.019 --> 00:02:42.310
Only the XS Max looked different because it
was obviously much larger, and that’s actually

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:45.220
the flagship model that most people upgraded
to.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:51.040
This year, the iPhone 11 Pro looks and feels
WAY different, with a brand new unique feeling

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:56.761
matte glass back, a relocated apple logo,
the new popular midnight green color, and

00:02:56.761 --> 00:03:02.010
most importantly, a very unique square camera
bump with large triple camera lenses that

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.540
really stand out.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:08.410
That new square bump with 3 lenses has become
a trademark alongside the Pro branding, so

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:14.489
now, it’s almost impossible to mistake the
11 Pro for the iPhone X or XS, unless you’re

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:16.030
looking at the front, of course.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:20.470
The 3rd thing that matters is that it sounds
different, and having the word Pro in the

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.299
name, is more unique than ever before.

00:03:23.299 --> 00:03:27.719
When I was standing in line at the Apple Store
on Launch day, I kept hearing regular people

00:03:27.719 --> 00:03:30.129
saying that they want the new iPhone Pro.

00:03:30.129 --> 00:03:33.930
They seemed like they didn’t really know
that much about tech, but what they did know

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.280
is that they wanted the Pro model.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.590
And throughout the weekend, I kept hearing
people ask, is that the new Pro?

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.450
Is that the iPhone Pro?

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:47.650
It seems as though the 11 part of the name
has faded away under the success of the Pro

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:48.650
name.

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:52.769
So it seems like using “Pro” is already
working for Apple’s benefit, even if some

00:03:52.769 --> 00:03:53.890
people disagree with it.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:54.890
And from a marketing standpoint, it totally
makes sense for Apple to do this.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:55.890
They could easily continue using this naming
scheme for years, and it actually works quite

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:56.890
well.

00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:57.890
I’ll explain why in a minute.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:58.890
Before I get into my personal thoughts on
what truly matters about the iPhone 11 Pro

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:04.010
and Pro Max, as well as the downsides or disappointments
of the Pro, I wanna quickly mention the real-world

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:08.680
differences and changes my wife noticed and
enjoyed about her new 11 Pro.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:14.390
First off, she loves the camera, especially
the new wider lens on the selfie camera, allowing

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:18.620
her to fit more into the frame without having
to stretch her hand out as far as she can.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:23.340
She also absolutely loves the new ultra-wide
lens, and she had a blast taking unique and

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.230
creative photos at the park.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:29.830
She was also really impressed with the video
stabilization, and she actually really likes

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:35.290
the square bump on the back compared to the
XS’s vertical bump, and she noticed much

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:36.460
better battery life as well.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:37.460
Her iPhone 11 Pro was still at 67% battery
life at 9:30pm on Sunday, with absolutely

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:38.460
zero charging throughout the day, which was
something that’s never happened to her before.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:41.030
In terms of performance, she didn’t really
notice a difference coming from the XS, but

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:45.550
she doesn’t really do any heavy tasks like
gaming or using professional apps or anything

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.550
like that.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:51.881
So overall, she’s very happy with her new
iPhone 11 Pro, even coming from the XS, so

00:04:51.881 --> 00:04:56.680
I think regular consumers who are coming from
an older iPhone will definitely notice a difference.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:02.040
Now let’s get into the real-world differences
that I, a tech enthusiast, noticed after spending

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.170
a few days with the 11 Pro Max.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:08.360
First of all, I am pleasantly surprised with
the battery life.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:11.700
Every time that I would check it, I’d be
surprised at how high it was compared to my

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:12.700
old XS Max.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:18.350
And on Sunday, I was at 61% battery life after
coming home at 9:30pm.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:22.870
This has never happened on my XS Max, so I
think the battery life is perhaps the biggest

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:24.400
deal with the new 11 Pro.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:29.830
And don’t take my word for it, Mrwhosetheboss
just released his battery drain test, and

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:34.720
even the smaller iPhone 11 Pro beat out the
Note 10 Plus, and that was with the Note 10

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:40.650
Plus manually set to a lower resolution than
both of the iPhones, at 1080P instead of the

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.640
1440P the Note is capable of.

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:49.090
And the iPhone 11 Pro Max lasted 8 hours and
32 minutes, the best battery life Mrwhosetheboss

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:51.300
has ever seen on any smartphone.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:54.960
As far as the design, I seriously can’t
get enough of it.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:59.470
The matte finish on the glass feels incredible
in the hand, and I’m shocked at how Apple

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:02.110
was able to pull off the square bump on the
back.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:07.780
It just looks so unique and premium compared
the vertical bump on the XS, and so far, everyone

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:09.710
else I know loves the new look.

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:14.050
The speakers have also been improved from
the XS Max, with the top and bottom speakers

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:18.670
being much more balanced than before, which
is why I think the new surround sound effect

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:19.750
works so well.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:23.930
As far as performance, I honestly haven’t
noticed a difference in the UI and using the

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:27.330
phone normally, but what most people don’t
really think about is that the reason the

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:31.950
cameras are as good as they are is solely
because of the extra performance of the new

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.290
A13 Bionic chip in the 11 Pro.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:38.240
That’s where most of the improvements are
going, and I’ll talk about them in just

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:39.240
a minute.

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:42.800
And even though a lot of the improvements
are geared towards efficiency, for getting

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:47.890
that awesome battery life, we actually saw
a huge improvement in raw performance in both

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:50.080
processor and graphics workloads.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:55.650
For gaming, the XS had excellent performance,
being able to max out the graphics on basically

00:06:55.650 --> 00:07:00.310
any game we tried, but it had a huge issue
while playing Fortnite at high brightness

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.220
at 60 frames per second.

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:06.560
After only 10 minutes, the XS would heat up
and the display would greatly dim.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:11.390
So I tried it on the 11 Pro Max and it was
able to last much longer before dimming, and

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:15.420
it didn’t dim nearly as much as before,
so I’m really impressed with the efficiency

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:20.430
of the new A13 chip, especially since you’ll
get better battery life during long gaming

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:21.430
sessions.

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:25.680
In my opinion, even if you can’t notice
the difference in performance right now, having

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:30.710
the extra power of the A13 for the next couple
of years is going to be a big deal for when

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:34.000
new apps and games come out that will actually
be able to use it, especially augmented reality

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.000
apps.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.640
And now let’s get into the cameras, the
main upgrade this year.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:41.480
We now get the ultra-wide lens, which is actually
really fun to use.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:45.430
The quality isn’t nearly as good as the
wide lens, but it’s a blast to get unique

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:46.900
angles and shots.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:51.900
The wide lens looks better than ever, with
excellent dynamic range and image quality.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.430
And I’m glad that Apple added a bit more
contrast to the photos so they don’t look

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:57.380
as flat as last year’s XS.

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:02.240
And the white balance looks very consistent
between lenses, whereas last year, it leaned

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.250
towards the warm side far too often.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:08.400
And for the telephoto lens, I’ve actually
noticed that photos taken with this lens turn

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:12.440
out better with less noise, especially for
portrait mode photos.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:15.870
However, I’m quite disappointed with portrait
blur edging.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:19.770
I thought they would improve on it this year,
but it still sucks when it comes to missing

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:21.580
large sections of background.

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:25.370
So I really hope Apple adds a time of flight
sensor next year.

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:30.770
Perhaps the biggest deal is Apple moving from
7 megapixels to 12 on the front facing camera,

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:32.950
as well as making the lens wider in general.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:38.800
It’s much more detailed than before and
being able to record 4K 60fps selfie video

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:39.800
is insane.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:44.779
And finally, Apple has added a night mode,
and it does such a great job, especially since

00:08:44.779 --> 00:08:49.930
the colors turn out natural and not oversaturated
like on a lot of the other Android phones.

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:53.620
The only downside is that you can’t use
night mode with the ultra-wide lens or the

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:56.050
selfie camera, which is a huge bummer.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:09:00.750
As for video recording, Apple has completely
knocked it out of the park with the 11 Pro.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:04.980
The quality looks incredible and beats out
basically every other phone on the market.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:08.360
And this year, the stabilization is absolutely
phenomenal.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:11.010
It just works so incredibly well.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:13.530
And I love how you can record with the ultra-wide
lens.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:18.579
But the biggest improvement for video recording
comes thanks to the A13 Bionic chip.

00:09:18.579 --> 00:09:23.640
You can now shoot at 4K 60 while getting extended
dynamic range, which means that the chip is

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:29.940
actually recording at 4K 120, with 60 darker
frames and 60 brighter frames, being blended

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:34.150
together in real-time to offer incredible
dynamic range.

00:09:34.150 --> 00:09:38.490
This is a huge deal and it puts an even bigger
gap between it and other smartphones.

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:42.620
However, there’s a massive downside with
recording.

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:46.640
While shooting in 4K 60, you can’t switch
between lenses.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:51.240
That means, if you start recording with the
ultra-wide lens, you can’t zoom out or switch

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:52.460
to another lens.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:56.790
It works perfectly fine while recording at
30 fps, but not at 60.

00:09:56.790 --> 00:10:01.200
That’s a major flaw especially now that
we have the added ultra-wide lens.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:05.810
But overall, the cameras are outstanding on
the 11 Pro, and we’ll be putting out some

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:09.991
very detailed camera comparisons shortly,
so if you’re not already subscribed, make

00:10:09.991 --> 00:10:12.750
sure to do so now so you don’t miss out!

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:16.890
So that leads me into a few things that I
found extremely disappointing this year.

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:22.360
Yes, the 11 Pro offers the most complete iPhone
package we’ve seen in years, and I honestly

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:26.400
think that most people who are on the edge
of upgrading should just do it unless they’re

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:30.610
perfectly happy with their current device,
but if we had these 3 things, I honestly think

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:32.230
it would be perfect.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:35.770
First off, the same 4GB of RAM on the 11 Pro?

00:10:35.770 --> 00:10:37.520
That’s just a bit sad.

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:43.980
And even worse, the same 64GB of storage at
the base price is just embarrassing, especially

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:50.360
since the Note 10 Plus comes with 256GB of
even faster storage at the same price.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:56.140
And finally, I was really hoping for an always-on
display on the 11 Pro, especially since Apple

00:10:56.140 --> 00:11:01.029
added it to their new Series 5 Apple Watch,
but we still don’t have it on the iPhone.

00:11:01.029 --> 00:11:06.370
Other than that, the iPhone 11 Pro is an excellent
package overall, and it looks and feels more

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:11.760
premium than ever before, making the 1000
dollar price honestly seem worth it again,

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:14.750
just like it was with the iPhone X from two
years ago.

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:18.650
This has been Vadim with Max Tech, and if
you enjoyed this review, make sure to check

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:23.680
out some of our other videos right there,
and click the circle above to subscribe for

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:24.820
our upcoming camera comparisons.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:27.330
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next one!

